ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dcb03ba9b0800f5a690cff435ec355b9bf90745056ab80e6cf55f8bbfd7e2cb0","event_uuid":"acee41ee-a366-47fd-a730-b78f9b1e84e1","position":{"commit_sha":"2800b41b47c4ed1ae10485de7c344818627adaa9","position":"1787084484566484001-acee41ee-a366-47fd-a730-b78f9b1e84e1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"55aed74b9855a9aa4397b77700a5a17ceb9adce86a81c46623bcd80dad585df7","event_uuid":"76867d6b-7e44-4b22-aacf-366e8c745459","position":{"commit_sha":"754db3859b7b41e03f3750bcd8c8433b4801c8b4","position":"1787086738127080269-76867d6b-7e44-4b22-aacf-366e8c745459"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787081599804901001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"76867d6b-7e44-4b22-aacf-366e8c745459","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4280-a3d6-bd7c-4b60"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`scripts/check_config_reads.py` proves every `_config_schema.py` field is consumed, but nothing proves the OPPOSITE: that ONLY approved composition roots / provider boundaries read ambient config and credentials — so a new below-seam `load_config`/`os.getenv` read, or a new credential name with no owner, can silently appear. `gen_env_registry.py` already implements AST env-read detection + one-level helper-shim resolution (`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`), and documents (bug b00f) that a helper ABSENT from that table is INVISIBLE. This gate REUSES that machinery, not a parallel copy.\n\n## Outcome\nA deterministic AST gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` (mirroring `check_config_reads.py`'s `check(root)->list[str]` / `main(argv)->int` contract and `# read-via: <pointer>` escape-marker style) that, for every `src/rebar` module NOT in the approved-seam set, flags each prohibited category below. An explicit registry enumerates approved seams and DERIVES its owner sets from existing registries (no duplicate). Test-only controls/protocol constants are allowed only via exact `path + symbol + rationale` entries (never path globs). An initial legacy-exception set enumerates current below-seam reads so the gate is introducible without touching product code; C3 (075b) drains it to empty.\n\n### Prohibited categories — concrete AST detection rules\nEach fires only when the enclosing module path is NOT an approved seam for that category. \"Resolved callee\" = after alias resolution (step 2).\n1. **Ambient env read** — reuse `gen_env_registry`'s matchers: `_is_os_environ` subscripted or `.get(...)`, and `os.getenv(...)` with a string-literal key. Resolved env-name captured for cats 5–6.\n2. **Helper-shim env read** — `Call` whose resolved callee is a key of `gen_env_registry.KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`; env-name resolved one level via that table's row (IMPORTED — single source). A shim-shaped callee (leading `_` + `env`/`pref`/`getenv`) ABSENT from the table, or any env read whose name arg is NOT a literal (dynamic), is reported `unresolved-env-read` — FAILS CLOSED (the doc-generator silently skips; closes b00f).\n3. **`load_config` call** — `Call` whose resolved callee is `load_config` (direct, `from ...config import load_config`, or local `lc = load_config; lc(...)`) in a module not an approved composition root.\n4. **Literal-`getattr` env equivalent** — `getattr(<recv>, <literal>, ...)` where `<recv>` resolves to `os.environ`; treated as cat 1 with the constant as env-name.\n5. **Provider-credential read** — a cat-1/2/4 read whose resolved env-name is in the credential set from `_child_env.owned_secret_names()`/`_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES`, outside the credential-boundary set.\n6. **Configurable adapter default / backend reload** — (a) a module-level assignment or function default-arg whose RHS is a prohibited access of cats 1–5; (b) a `_backend_registry` selector/accessor call (`select_backend`, `register`, or direct `_REGISTRY` read) below an approved provider boundary.\n\n### Approved seams (two DISTINCT sets) + owner-registry derivation\nOwner sets are DERIVED at run time from existing registries, not hand-copied:\n- **Composition roots** (own cats 1–4 config reads): `*/config.py`, `_config_sources.py`, `_child_env.py`, and LLM model adapters `anthropic_model.py`/`bedrock_model.py` (own LLM env — NOT JIRA credentials).\n- **Provider-credential boundaries** (own cat-5 reads): `_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py`, `.../access_check.py`, `.../adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py`, `.../adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` (all under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`) — the real readers of `JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_PAT` (per docs/env-vars.md), enumerated as approved owners (C3 handles how they SOURCE it; not a legacy exception).\n- **Credential names** ← `_child_env.owned_secret_names()` (union of `_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES`), mapped to owner adapter + boundary.\n- **Adapters/backends** ← an AST scan for `@register(<literal>)` decorators under `_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/` (static, offline). NOT `_backend_registry._REGISTRY`, which is EMPTY at plain import time (adapters self-register only via the lazy `import rebar_reconciler.adapters` inside `select_backend`).\n- **Declared-env baseline** ← union of `gen_env_registry.scan(src/rebar)` names and `_deprecations.REGISTRY(kind==\"env\")`. \"Newly declared\" = a spelling/credential name the scan surfaces that maps to NO owner → gate fails naming it.\n\n## Plan\n1. **Reuse, don't re-implement.** Import `scan`/`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`/`_is_os_environ`/`_str_literal` directly from `gen_env_registry.py` (single source; no shared-module extraction). Cats 3/4/6 and receiver-aliasing (step 2) add new logic on top.\n2. **Alias + receiver resolution** per module: (a) callee aliases (`import ... as`, `from ... import name`, local `x = <callee>`) so direct/import/local-aliased call forms resolve to one canonical callee; (b) receiver-object aliases — a local bound to `os.environ` directly OR conditionally (`src = os.environ if env is None else env`) — so `src.get(<literal>)`/`src[<literal>]` classifies as a cat-1 ambient/credential read (closes the `src = os.environ; src.get('SECRET')` evasion, e.g. access_check.py's `JIRA_API_TOKEN` read).\n3. **Approved-seam + owner registry**: enumerate the two seam sets and derive owner sets as specified above; reject path-glob exceptions STRUCTURALLY (any exception `path` with a glob metachar or naming a directory).\n4. **Diagnostic** reports `path`, `symbol`, `access kind`, `owning seam` (or UNOWNED).\n5. **Legacy-exception set**: exact `path+symbol+rationale` entries for current below-seam reads; C3 drains to empty.\n6. **Fixtures + self-tests** (see Testing).\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Synthetic fixtures for direct/import-aliased/local-aliased forms and EACH category 1–6 (incl. `getattr(os.environ,...)`, a receiver-aliased credential read, an unresolved dynamic read, a shim-shaped call absent from the table, a credential read outside its boundary, a below-seam `select_backend`) each fail with the expected `path/symbol/access-kind/owning-seam` diagnostic.\n- Self-tests: a new bypass, a new unowned name (`_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES` addition or new env spelling), a path-glob exception, or a missing rationale each fail. The unowned-name case doubles as the drift self-test.\n- Clean approved fixtures pass with no findings.\n- Runs OFFLINE, no network/CI: `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` exits 0 on the current tree, 1 on a synthetic violation.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nAdditive: not wired into `make lint`/CI (C2, 735b); product code unchanged (C3, 075b). Importing `gen_env_registry.py`'s scanner leaves its `--check` output unchanged. Rollback deletes the new script/registry/fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of the 6 categories has a concrete AST rule (per Outcome) with a synthetic fixture (direct/import-aliased/local-aliased) failing with `path`, `symbol`, `access kind`, owning seam; clean approved fixtures pass.\n- [ ] Env-read detection + shim resolution REUSE `gen_env_registry`'s `scan`/`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` (direct import), not a parallel parser; receiver-object aliasing (`src = os.environ ...; src.get(...)`) is detected; a shim-shaped callee absent from the table and a dynamic env read fail CLOSED as `unresolved-env-read`.\n- [ ] The owner registry DERIVES credential names from `_child_env`, backend keys from a static `@register(<literal>)` decorator scan (NOT the import-time-empty `_REGISTRY`), env baseline from `gen_env_registry.scan` + `_deprecations.REGISTRY(kind==\"env\")`; the provider-credential boundary set is enumerated distinctly from composition roots; a newly declared spelling/credential name lacking an owner fails (drift self-test); path-glob exceptions rejected structurally.\n- [ ] Exposes `check(root)->list[str]` and `main(argv)->int`, is unit-tested, runs offline with no CI/network dependency, exits 0 on the current tree (legacy-exception set covers current reads; C3 drains it).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"NEW AST ownership gate + approved-owner/seam registry."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership.py","reason":"NEW unit tests for gate contract + registry."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py","reason":"NEW held-out red-proof fixtures + bypass self-tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4"],["relates_to","4280-a3d6-bd7c-4b60"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4","parent_status_uuid":"888a993a-bb13-4ed8-bbc2-3d54e8dfd9d0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.1 — Config-ownership AST gate + approved-owner registry + red-proof fixtures","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a847227d-36ef-4563-ae48-7d92d5b8b822","5b62f031-4ba0-46c3-a68b-28fb8c0424c7","24c3aa71-9b5e-4a65-bc7c-3cb77a28d62c","35eeb8fd-3cc9-4317-b5d6-06332d9ce598","87c82c2a-5bdc-4b8a-8bff-fc3c1806ab8e","fba12460-92d0-46df-aa89-b50457aa1475","7c316fbb-fb9a-4062-9ad2-683ce6a1f446","55d53880-adf1-41f2-80f6-4763d42a85fc","820c63de-69d1-442c-b53e-8212b98a7f59","888a993a-bb13-4ed8-bbc2-3d54e8dfd9d0","acee41ee-a366-47fd-a730-b78f9b1e84e1","76867d6b-7e44-4b22-aacf-366e8c745459"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787086738127080270,"uuid":"6aa5b486-9d56-47e6-a067-bd112110ca66"}